      "writtenOn": "2022-07-27T15:46:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we get `ALERT_STORM_MAX_COUNT` interrupts within `ALERT_STORM_INTERVAL`, we will reset the port to stop the interrupts. This is to avoid spending too much time in the interrupt task and triggering the watchdog timer.\n\nCurrently, the threshold is 480 interrupts in 1 second.\n\nI would be curious to know what the actual interrupt rate is during the fastest/longest BIST test and what actually happens with the watchdog timer during that test if we don\u0027t reset the port. Naturally, that would be somewhat hardware-specific.",
      "parentUuid": "6c90cf19_9eb4c12b",
      "revId": "3d71ad3dc69839850dc52f43d5d01de130cdbe47",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
